{
 "about": "Trial of the niratl recipe (telluric parameters from solar-clean pixels, HITRAN H2O shifts, solar broadening; line coupling kept on files 4 and 5) on sampled windows of the other Kitt Peak files, at several pressure-width scales, 2026-10-18. Windows: every 15th (1983 pair), every 10th (1990 files). 'old' is the canonical run. Written by scripts/score_telluric_correction.py --relative-transmission; file 5 is also scored against photatl, the authors' correction of the same spectrum.",
 "files": {
  "ftsspec_830626_2": {
   "method": "niratl ships the authors' own corrected solar spectrum (Wallace, Hinkle & Livingston 1993). Ours minus theirs mixes both corrections' errors, so instead each is scored on its own, the same way: at pixels where the model transmission is below 0.97 and the solar model is flat (above 0.995 of its continuum), the rms of the corrected spectrum about a running mean of nearby pixels with neither solar nor telluric absorption. A perfect correction leaves noise there. The first and last 50 pixels are not scored: an edge pixel is inside the neighbouring page too (pages overlap by 5 cm-1), and a fit that leaves edges out should not be judged on them. Two bins: every telluric pixel (T < 0.97) and the deep ones (T < 0.7).",
   "settings": {
    "stem": "ftsspec_830626_2",
    "authors": "none",
    "relative_transmission": true
   },
